<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis the Pious</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis the Pious was the son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>, ruling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> from 814 to 840. His attempts to arrange the succession among his sons provoked rebellions and civil wars. After his death the empire was divided among his sons by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-verdun">Treaty of Verdun</a> in 843.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious.jpg" alt="Louis the Pious" width="318" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludwik_I_Pobo%C5%BCny.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
